# Rank certificates separating two native pure four-groups

The product of the displacements of masks 818 and 1449 has rank 20,
whereas the marked pair in census row 2 has rank 16. Packed products and
two row-span certificates establish these claims over the actual binary
112-dimensional representation. This provides an invariant for the two
pure rows of the native centralizer census, without a printed MOG marking.

Source: Kleidman--Wilson (1988), Table 1, p.487, motivates the two pure
rows. The native ATLAS word conventions are those of `KernelCount` and
`LocalInvolutionCensus`. The untrusted witness generator is retained in
`Scratch/J4PureTwoA/generate_native_pair.py`.
-/

